## 7.1 Docker Fundamentals

### What is Docker?

Docker is a platform for developing, shipping, and running applications inside **containers**. A container is a lightweight, standalone executable package that includes everything needed to run the software: code, runtime, system tools, system libraries, and settings.

### Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Image** | Read-only template with instructions for creating a container. Built via `Dockerfile`. |
| **Container** | Running instance of an image. Isolated but shares the host OS kernel. |
| **Dockerfile** | Text file containing commands to assemble an image. `docker build` reads it. |
| **Docker Compose** | Tool for defining and running multi-container Docker applications via `docker-compose.yml`. |
| **Registry** | Storage and distribution system for Docker images (GHCR, Docker Hub, ECR, Artifactory). |
| **Layer** | Each `Dockerfile` instruction creates a layer; layers are cached for faster rebuilds. |
| **Tag** | Name identifier for an image (e.g., `api-gateway:v1.2.3` or `api-gateway:latest`). |

### Docker vs. Virtual Machines

| Aspect | Docker | Virtual Machine |
|--------|--------|-----------------|
| **Guest OS** | Shares host kernel | Full guest OS |
| **Startup time** | Seconds | Minutes |
| **Size** | MBs (image layers) | GBs (full OS) |
| **Isolation** | Process-level | Hardware-level |
| **Portability** | High (same kernel) | Lower (hypervisor-dependent) |

### Docker Image Lifecycle

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Write Dockerfile] --> B[docker build]
    B --> C[Image created (layered)]
    C --> D[docker push <registry>]
    D --> E[docker pull <registry>]
    E --> F[docker run]
    F --> G[Container running]
    G --> H[docker stop]
    H --> I[docker rm]
    I --> J[Image remains in registry]
```

## 7.2 Dockerfile Best Practices

### Minimalist `Dockerfile` Pattern

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1
FROM node:22-alpine AS base

# 1ï¸âƒ£ Set working directory
WORKDIR /usr/src/app

# 2ï¸âƒ£ Install dependencies (layer cached if package.json unchanged)
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci --omit=dev

# 3ï¸âƒ£ Add source code (layer changes on every commit â†’ put last)
COPY src/ ./src/

# 4ï¸âƒ£ Build TypeScript (production artifacts)
RUN npx tsc -b

# 5ï¸âƒ£ Expose application port
EXPOSE 3000

# 6ï¸âƒ£ Start the server
CMD ["node", "dist/src/app.js"]
```

### Multi-Stage Build (Recommended for Production)

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1
# ---- Stage 1: Build ----
FROM node:22-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /usr/src/app
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .
RUN npx tsc -b

# ---- Stage 2: Runtime ----
FROM node:22-alpine AS base
WORKDIR /usr/src/app
# Copy only built artifacts from builder
COPY --from=builder /usr/src/app/dist ./dist
COPY package.json ./
RUN npm ci --omit=dev
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "dist/src/app.js"]
```

### `.dockerignore` (Mirror of `.gitignore`)

```text
node_modules
dist
.github
*.log
*.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.travis.yml
.travis.yml
.env*
.git/
.vscode/
```

**Why?** Excludes unnecessary files from build context, reducing image size and build time.

## 7.3 `docker compose` for Local Development

### `docker-compose.yml`

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  api-gateway:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    environment:
      - REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
      - JWT_SECRET=${JWT_SECRET}
    depends_on:
      - redis
    volumes:
      - ./src:/usr/src/app/src:ro
    restart: unless-stopped

  redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine
    ports:
      - "6379:6379"
    restart: unless-stopped

  nginx:
    image: nginx:stable-alpine
    ports:
      - "80:80"
      - "443:443"
    volumes:
      - ./nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:ro
    depends_on:
      - api-gateway
    restart: unless-stopped
```

### Common `docker compose` commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `docker compose up -d` | Start all services in detached mode |
| `docker compose down` | Stop and remove containers, networks, volumes |
| `docker compose logs` | View output from all services |
| `docker compose exec <service> <cmd>` | Run a command inside a running service |
| `docker compose ps` | List running services |
| `docker compose build` | Rebuild images (without starting containers) |
| `docker compose pull` | Pull image versions without creating containers |

### Health Checks

```yaml
services:
  api-gateway:
    ...
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost:3000/healthz"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 10s
      retries: 3
      start_period: 10s
```
